   "notes": "An upper-division Comparative Literature course taught by a Slavic faculty member may be used as 4 units of electives. Courses dealing with East-Central Europe or Russia, in areas such as Anthropology, Film and Media Studies, Global Studies, History, Music, Political Science, and Theater and Dance may be accepted by petition after consultation with the department advisor (8 units maximum).\nUpper-division courses taught in Russian taken through other UCs may be applied to the major by petition after consultation with the department advisor.\nA year of study abroad on UCEAP, or another program, in a Russian-speaking country is highly recommended."
